  "notes": "v247 — MANIFEST-PTI (owner, Oct 22, 2026 20:04 MDT + Oct 23): the manifest is the full day record — dispatch, GPS route, PTI, summary — but it carried no PTI at all: Oct 22 HAD both inspections filed (pre 07:24 @ 169,888, post 17:21 @ 170,079) and the printed manifest showed none of it, because collect() never read pti_reports. Fix (modules/manifest.js): collect now reads the day's PTI reports (latest filing of each kind; the v242 profile fence in the app's own stamping — an unstamped record belongs to p1) and returns them as manifest facts: time, odometer reading, defects result, filed/signed status. A new PTI section (its own remembered toggle, default on, like every section) prints both rows in the document and the screen preview — a side never filed says \"Not filed\". Completeness is now a printed fact: a manifest is COMPLETE only with PTI (pre + post) AND the GPS trail on file; a closed day that lacks a piece closes with \"Manifest incomplete — missing: …\" naming the pieces, and a complete day says so. A day still in progress makes no completeness claim. An unsigned filing counts as filed — its row shows \"Filed — not signed\" honestly. Harness: tools/manifest-pti-v247-test.js on the Oct 22 fixture — RED 19/19 (no PTI anywhere), GREEN 19/19; every manifest suite holds. PIN MOVES (cited): ?v=246 index cohort (26) + standing webVersion/?v= pins in the suites move 246 -> 247. Native unchanged (v43 shell + iPhone web pick it up). Machine-green is preparation — the verdict is his: Oct 22's manifest shows both inspections and reads Manifest complete.",
